# 14. Alternative Approaches

# Approach 1 — Recommended

Application fetches secrets dynamically.

Most common production approach.

---

# Approach 2 — Startup Script

Shell script fetches secret BEFORE app starts.

Example:

```bash
SECRET=$(aws secretsmanager get-secret-value ...)
```

Then:

```bash
export DB_PASSWORD=...
```

Less preferred.

---

# Approach 3 — ECS Native Secrets

AWS ECS can inject secrets automatically.

Example:

```json
"secrets": [
  {
    "name": "DB_PASSWORD",
    "valueFrom": "arn:aws:secretsmanager:..."
  }
]
```

This is ECS feature.

NOT normal Docker Compose.

---

# 15. Security Best Practices

GOOD:

```text
Use IAM Roles + AWS Secrets Manager
```

BAD:

```dockerfile
ENV DB_PASSWORD=secret123
```

Why bad?

Because secrets become visible in:

* Docker image layers
* docker inspect
* logs
* GitHub

---

# Best Production Pattern

```text
Docker Compose
      ↓
Passes SECRET_NAME only
      ↓
Backend App Fetches Actual Secret
```

---

# Why Enterprises Prefer Runtime Secret Fetching

Benefits:

* automatic rotation
* centralized management
* auditing
* encryption
* no hardcoded secrets
* latest secret always used

